# 4.2 THE IF-ELSE STATEMENT

An `if-else` statement executes one block of statements if its Boolean expression is true, or another block if its Boolean expression is false.

It has two parts:

1. The `if` clause.
2. The `else` clause.

### General Format

```csharp
if (expression)
{
    statements;
}
else
{
    statements;
}
```

The `if` block executes when the expression is true. The `else` block executes when the expression is false.

